<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="The Portfolio–Paycheck Gap Index compares US stock-market growth with median full-time paycheck growth since 1980."
    >
    <title>Portfolio–Paycheck Gap Index · $period</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/site.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to the indicator</a>

    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Portfolio–Paycheck Gap Index home">
        <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">P/P</span>
        <span>Portfolio–Paycheck Gap</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#history">History</a>
        <a href="#interpretation">Interpret</a>
        <a href="#resources">Resources</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main" data-latest-quarter="$period_code">
      <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">United States · Quarterly · 1980 Q1 = 100</p>
          <h1 id="page-title">When markets compound faster than paychecks</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            PPG compares the growth of a broad US stock-market investment with
            the growth of the median full-time paycheck. It measures relative
            paths—not a dollar gap, valuation, or typical worker portfolio.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="data/ppg.csv" download>Download the data</a>
            <a class="button" href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap/blob/main/methodology/v0.1.md">Read methodology v$methodology_version</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="reading-card" aria-label="Latest PPG reading">
          <div class="reading-meta">
            <p>Latest complete quarter</p>
            <span class="status status-$status_class" data-state="$status_class">$status_label</span>
          </div>
          <p class="reading-value" aria-label="$value index points">$value</p>
          <p class="reading-unit">index points · through $period</p>
          <dl class="change-grid">
            <div>
              <dt>Quarterly</dt>
              <dd>$qoq</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Annual</dt>
              <dd>$yoy</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="status-note status-note-$status_class"><strong>$status_label.</strong> $status_note</p>
          <p class="as-of">Quarter ended <time datetime="$observation_date_iso">$observation_date</time></p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="section chart-section" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">The long view</p>
            <h2 id="history-title">$observation_count quarters of relative growth</h2>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="data/ppg.svg">Open chart as SVG <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="chart-card">
          <img
            src="data/ppg.svg"
            width="1200"
            height="675"
            alt="Line chart of quarterly PPG history from $first_period through $period. Exact observations are available in the linked CSV."
          >
          <figcaption>
            PPG level, quarterly from $first_period to $period. The baseline is
            100 in 1980 Q1. <a href="data/ppg.csv">Download exact observations</a>.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="interpretation" aria-labelledby="interpretation-title">
        <div class="section-heading narrow-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Read the ratio</p>
            <h2 id="interpretation-title">Large number, specific meaning</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            The level compares two growth factors from the same base. It is not
            itself a percentage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="component-grid" aria-label="Latest component index values">
          <article class="component-card component-market">
            <p class="component-label">Market component</p>
            <p class="component-value">$market_component</p>
            <p>Hypothetical broad-market wealth, rebased to 100.</p>
          </article>
          <div class="ratio-mark" aria-hidden="true">÷</div>
          <article class="component-card component-paycheck">
            <p class="component-label">Paycheck component</p>
            <p class="component-value">$paycheck_component</p>
            <p>Median weekly earnings, rebased to 100.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="explain-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="step">01</span>
            <h3>Start at 100</h3>
            <p>Both components equal 100 in 1980 Q1. The base is a measuring reference, not a claim about fairness.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="step">02</span>
            <h3>Compare growth</h3>
            <p>Above 100 means market wealth grew faster; below 100 means the paycheck grew faster over the same span.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="step">03</span>
            <h3>Keep claims narrow</h3>
            <p>PPG does not show who owns stocks, explain causation, measure living costs, or forecast either series.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <aside class="callout">
          <p class="callout-title">The populations are different.</p>
          <p>
            The market leg is a hypothetical investment. The paycheck leg is a
            changing cross-sectional median for full-time wage and salary
            workers. PPG does not imply that those workers own the portfolio.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap/blob/main/docs/interpretation-guide.md">Use the interpretation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="section resources" id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
        <div class="section-heading narrow-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Open materials</p>
            <h2 id="resources-title">Inspect every layer</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Data vintage $snapshot_id · generated $generated_date</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resource-grid">
          <a href="data/ppg.csv">
            <span>CSV</span>
            <strong>Quarterly history</strong>
            <small>Values and components</small>
          </a>
          <a href="data/latest.json">
            <span>JSON</span>
            <strong>Latest reading</strong>
            <small>Value, changes, and status</small>
          </a>
          <a href="data/provenance.json">
            <span>JSON</span>
            <strong>Provenance</strong>
            <small>Sources, dates, and checksums</small>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap/blob/main/methodology/v0.1.md">
            <span>MD</span>
            <strong>Methodology</strong>
            <small>Definition and limitations</small>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap#reproduce-and-validate">
            <span>CLI</span>
            <strong>Reproduce</strong>
            <small>Build from source data</small>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap/releases">
            <span>GH</span>
            <strong>Releases</strong>
            <small>Named, immutable vintages</small>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>
        An open, reproducible economic indicator. Methodology v$methodology_version ·
        snapshot <code>$snapshot_id</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        JKP-derived data and charts are limited to noncommercial use under CC
        BY-NC 4.0. <a href="https://github.com/oddurs/portfolio-paycheck-gap/blob/main/DATA_LICENSE.md">Attribution and terms</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
